From 7ae59acf25c0c476d12d479c509ee07247c3537c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:37:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui): reach split-module helpers through server so
 turn-end outcome refresh works [daveey]

turn_outcome.py imported _session_db straight from session_workdir. Split modules are written
against server.py's globals (bind_module rebinds them there), so the raw module copy raised
NameError: _get_db on every Desktop/TUI turn end and the chat's stored outcome never refreshed.
The test hid it by stubbing session_workdir._get_db (raising=False), which only the test had.

- turn_outcome, kanban_unloaded, notice_guarantee, kanban_remote_notices, methods_bot_relay now
  call server._name for split helpers. The same bug made session_notifications._readopt_wake_profiles
  (raw copy: NameError on Path, swallowed) return only the launch store, so the unloaded sweep and
  the notice guarantee never searched named profiles' stores.
- test_turn_outcome_refresh: drop the session_workdir._get_db stub; add
  test_refresh_uses_server_bound_session_db (red before: NameError).
- test_split_module_imports: AST guard failing on any direct import of a bind_module split
  module's function from another tui_gateway module.
- kanban_unloaded busy/wake tests patch server's helpers (the real call path) instead of the
  module copies, which were inert after the fix.
